      "findings": [
        {
          "id": "D1-RA-001",
          "severity": "blocking",
          "blockingAuthority": "author",
          "title": "reference native types 正确，但完整 Change / Delivery 生命周期内容被压缩丢失",
          "problem": "053 approved Design/Spec 明确要求长期 reference visualizations 表达 Change complete lifecycle 与 Delivery complete lifecycle，并允许旧 preview content 作为 authoring input；055 最终 `change-lifecycle.workflow.json` 的主图仅有 explore/propose/apply gate/apply verify/review close/archive checkpoint 6 个聚合节点，把三个明确 review action、三个 revise action及其 blocker-authority re-review 路径压进 sublabel/cards；`delivery-lifecycle.lifecycle.json` 主图仅有 Start/Changes/Ready+Full Test/Actual+Compare/Finalize+Final 5 个聚合状态，把 Full Test failure → Delivery Finding → Owner decision → corrective Change → checkpoint → fresh Ready/fresh Full Test authorization 等闭环仅写在 cards。两文件虽然 Archify validate/deliver PASS，但“renderer-valid”不等于“complete lifecycle visualization”。",
          "contractRef": "053 approved Design Goals/Decision 2 and flowkit-architecture-assets spec: long-lived reference visualization sources for the complete Change and Delivery lifecycles; human review presentation order = Change complete lifecycle → Delivery complete lifecycle → Current → Planned",
          "invariant": "长期 reference 可以是非权威 projection，但既然被命名并冻结为 complete lifecycle visualization，其主图结构必须足以让人/AI直接看到正式生命周期关键 Action/gate/loop；不得把决定流程理解的 review/revise 或 failure/corrective loop 仅降级为卡片注释。Formal facts 仍是 authority，但 visualization 必须忠实投影这些 facts。",
          "requiredOutcome": "Revise Apply while preserving the native Archify physical contract (`workflow` for Change, `lifecycle` for Delivery) and the non-authoritative reference boundary. Expand the reference graph structures so the complete canonical lifecycle is visible in the visualization itself, not only in notes/cards. Strengthen D1 regression coverage enough that future simplification cannot silently remove the required lifecycle steps/loops. Do not revert to `.sequence.json`, do not make reference authoritative, and do not change Current/Planned/E1 boundaries.",
          "acceptance": [
            "Change workflow visibly represents explore → review-explore → author-only revise-explore/re-review boundary → propose → review-propose → author-only revise-propose/re-review → Owner apply authorization → apply → Change Verification → review-apply → author-only revise-apply/reverification/re-review → Owner archive authorization → archive → completed → separate Git Change Checkpoint boundary. Equivalent native-workflow structuring is acceptable; exact layout is not prescribed.",
            "Change visualization makes `changes-requested ≠ revise-required` and Owner/Verification/External blocker stop-boundary semantics visible without requiring the reader to infer the whole lifecycle only from a card.",
            "Delivery lifecycle visibly represents Delivery Start/Current+Planned → required Changes+Checkpoints → Ready → Owner Full Test authorization → passed/failed split; failed path reaches Delivery Finding → Owner decision → optional corrective Change → ordinary Change lifecycle/checkpoint → fresh Ready/fresh authorization; passed path reaches Actual/Compare → architecture acceptance/Owner finalize authorization → Delivery Final → Merge/next Current source as applicable to the frozen reference scope.",
            "Both updated files remain `diagram_type=workflow|lifecycle`, exact managed Archify 2.14.0 validate+deliver PASS, and `architecture/reference/**` remains a stale-able projection with formal facts winning conflicts.",
            "D1 tests assert the presence/structure of the key complete-lifecycle steps/loops in addition to merely asserting Archify renderability; Current/Planned JSON, thin CLI, Verification mapping and HTML-ignore boundaries remain green."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
